## Fifteen puzzle (fifteen-puzzle), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   5. If a block is adjacent to a clear location then you can move the block onto the clear location.
##   6. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   7. If a location is next to an object but it is not diagonal with the object then it is adjacent to the object.
##   9. The goal is that there are fifteen matching locations.
##  11. If the value of a location is the value of the block that is on the location then the location is matching.
## World: init-i15puzzle.world (a 4 by 4 grid; fifteen numbered blocks)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator slide-block (argument1 = the block, argument2 = the clear location), statement 5; adjacent (statement 7) is a
##     static relation between locations, a block being adjacent to what its location is adjacent to (A-G1); clear is a
##     maintained one-argument relation (statement 6).
##   - The goal is expanded over the blocks of the world file: every block is on the location with its value (A-G3).
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute location 32
production optimize-attribute block 32
production optimize-attribute task 32
production optimize-attribute object 32
production optimize-attribute on 15
production optimize-attribute below 15
production optimize-attribute clear 16
production optimize-attribute adjacent 48


## Propose initialize-fifteen-puzzle when its conditions below hold.
sp {fifteen-puzzle*propose*initialize-fifteen-puzzle
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-fifteen-puzzle ^task-operator false)
}

sp {fifteen-puzzle*apply*initialize-fifteen-puzzle
